            "anno" : "Signal peptide of G",
            "bit_cutoff" : 36,
            "comment" : "Predicted with SignalP 6.0 -- which IS installed on this machine; the first build wrongly recorded it as unavailable, and it then failed because its model_weights directory was empty until the weights were restored from the licensed tarball already on disk. Six of seven G clusters predict a signal peptide at p = 0.80-0.97 cleaving after residue 19-25, and apply_signalp.py verified each cut against its cluster's own members (first mature residue modal at 98-100%). THREE SEPARATE GATES then cut the feature back to what is trustworthy. (1) Cluster 7 was withheld by apply_signalp itself: its profile recalls its own training sequences at 20.5 bits, below the 30-bit floor a caller needs. (2) Clusters 4 and 5 are withheld here, in Alignments/.../G_SP/withheld/, because their profiles disagree with GP_N about where the mature protein starts and called signal peptides of up to 52 aa. (3) bit_cutoff is 36 by measurement: calls scoring 39.6-56.2 bits put the GP_N start exactly one base after the G_SP end, every time, while calls at 25.7-31.5 bits drift by 3-15 nt. The result is a feature that calls on about a third of genomes and is exact wherever it calls. It remains a PREDICTION: no bornavirus signal peptide has been determined experimentally.",
