            "anno" : "RNA-dependent RNA polymerase",
            "comment" : "L is a SPLICED feature, and the junction is the literature's. Walker 2000 (PMID 10756058) states it for strain V / NC_001607 verbatim: transcription unit III initiates at nt 1889, intron II spans nt 2410-3703, and its removal 'results in fusion of 17 nt to the 5' end of the conserved sequence at nt 3704 and provides an in-frame AUG (nt 2393)', giving the 1,711 aa, 190 kDa protein that paper precipitates from infected cells. Measured independently here by requiring an EXACT match of each deposited L to its own genome: 107 orthobornavirus junctions round-trip with a canonical GT..AG donor/acceptor, a 17-18 nt first exon and an intron of 1,282-1,294 nt -- the published intron II is 1,294 nt, so the measurement reproduces the paper. The spliced product begins MSFHAS in strain V (exon 1 gives M-S-F-H-A plus two nucleotides, and the hybrid sixth codon is completed by the first base of exon 2); some lineages read MSFHAR because that base differs. L is COLLINEAR in Carbovirus, Cultervirus and Cartilovirus (11 of 11 deposits), so those genera get references with a zero-length intron, which makes the spliced caller return the collinear ORF and keeps the family on one feature. A PSSM CDS was tried first and rejected: it put up to 46 spurious residues on the orthobornavirus N-terminus. The 1,608 aa (nt 3996) and 1,558 aa (nt 4146) internal-start forms are NOT modelled -- Walker 2000 looked for the 170 kDa one in infected cells and did not find it.",
